  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nAs per [this DOM issue](https://github.com/whatwg/dom/issues/1407) `.attachShadow` was changed to use the global registry by default rather than the host's. However this change isn't reflected in the [serialization steps](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#serialising-html-fragments) of shadow roots in the HTML spec:\n\n> If current node's [custom element registry](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#element-custom-element-registry) is not shadow's [custom element registry](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#shadowroot-custom-element-registry), then append \" shadowrootcustomelementregistry=\"\"\".\n\nI believe the change here should be to simply to [check the current node's document' registry](https://github.com/Jamesernator/html/commit/200117d92c358b7105b87a0283e69db7b711ce91) instead.",
